WEBVTT

00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:10.970
It's splendid. Growth
beyond what we'd expected.

00:00:10.970 --> 00:00:13.220
Having synchronized with Kaito Daimon,

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:16.860
the Armlet of Orpheus has had its reactions amplified.

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:20.130
Everything's gone as
you expected, Mr. Rook.

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:24.420
We will move the project
to the next sequence.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.760
But, ain't it a little early for that?

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:31.900
If we did that and something
were to happen to Kaito Daimon...

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:34.800
Shouldn't we first ask what
Count Pythagoras thinks?

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:38.640
Sir.

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:49.000
You're dashing when you're
solving puzzles...

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:51.490
Kaito.

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:04.500
Kaito.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:06.550
Kaito?

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:08.630
KAITO!

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:13.050
Get up, you friggin' lazybones!

00:01:35.530 --> 00:01:37.820
Kimi no nounai e to shinnyuu
Gonna infiltrate your brain

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:40.570
Nemutteru suki ni baby, open the gate
While you're sleeping, baby, open the gate

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:42.410
Fukuzatsusugi security
Too-complicated security

00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:45.160
Kakusareru to abakitakunaru
When something's hidden, it makes me want to expose it

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:49.670
Barabara ni chirabatte iru password o hiroiatsume
I'll gather up those loose, scattered passwords

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:54.380
Kakushin ni sematte yuku, sono shoutai o misete
And approach the core, so show me that true form

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:56.590
Kantan ni clear dekinai
I can't clear it easily

00:01:56.590 --> 00:01:59.260
Saki nante motto yomenai
Can read what lies ahead even less

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:01.260
Kaidoku fukanou smile
A smile that can't be deciphered

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:03.560
Kiken na puzzle
A dangerous puzzle

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:05.470
Lock sareteta door aru nara
If there's a door that's been locked

00:02:05.470 --> 00:02:08.310
Zutto tataite miru beki, kaza-ana hiraku wa
You must keep striking it, a crack will open

00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:12.820
Eien ni hodokenai nazo nanka wa nai
No mystery remains unsolved forever

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:15.110
Makiokosu, it's a supernova!
It's forming, it's a supernova!

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:19.780
Tobikiri shigekiteki na hirameki o agemashou
I will give you thoroughly stimulating insight

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:22.030
Misskey-misskey la-tu-ma

00:02:22.030 --> 00:02:24.370
Yume no naka, it's a supernova!
In the middle of a dream, it's a supernova!

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:27.000
Watashi wa, sou, brain diver
I am, yes, a brain diver

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:32.880
Kimi ga sagashimotometeru kotae ni nareru made
Until I become familiar with the answer you seek

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:38.550
Brain diver

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:43.350
Brain diver

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:52.020
Puzzle Time at Reunion

00:02:57.270 --> 00:03:01.030
Ow... The hell kind of
way was that to wake me?

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:03.310
YOU were the one who wouldn't get up!

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:06.040
Yeah, thanks for the unbearable injury.

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:07.380
YOU SAY SOMETHING?

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:23.550
No. I, Ana, will solve it.

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:27.600
Both Cubik and Ana have changed,

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:30.560
choosing to act alongside Kaito.

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:33.410
Their talents as Phi-Brain children

00:03:33.410 --> 00:03:36.740
may have begun to awaken.

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:41.780
Kaito, too, has grown
remarkably as a Solver.

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:43.240
There have been times, principal,

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:45.820
I've thought your approach
was too dangerous.

00:03:46.630 --> 00:03:48.080
But...

00:03:48.890 --> 00:03:50.340
What's the matter?

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:54.780
We've discussed Herbert Mueller
having been forced out, yes?

00:03:54.780 --> 00:03:58.050
Yes. You said the former person
in charge had returned.

00:03:59.350 --> 00:04:00.640
Please look at this.

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:05.550
Written orders from POG Japan?

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:08.560
This is...!

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:11.090
Good morning!

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:13.040
'Sup?

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:17.250
What's that?

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:18.200
Dunno.

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:20.770
It was up there when we arrived.

00:04:20.770 --> 00:04:22.070
Graffiti?

00:04:22.430 --> 00:04:24.400
It's not like we're kids.

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:26.830
Wait!

00:04:36.020 --> 00:04:37.080
Kaito?

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:49.570
It was a puzzle?

00:04:49.570 --> 00:04:50.430
This is...

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:52.900
This puzzle is...!

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:01.950
You remembered, didn't you?

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:19.920
Or have you forgotten me?

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:23.740
How could I?

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:26.220
How could I forget?

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:34.210
Your condition's better?

00:05:34.590 --> 00:05:36.730
Yeah. You look good too, Kaito.

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:40.490
Your uniform... Is that
Crossfield Academy?

00:05:40.490 --> 00:05:42.240
I'll be going back soon enough.

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:44.180
For now, I'm going to a high school.

00:05:44.180 --> 00:05:45.750
Crossfield Academy?

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:48.110
That school with
geniuses from all over the world?

00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:50.750
Kaito knows someone like that?!

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:54.870
Huh? So... Hey, Kaito!

00:05:54.870 --> 00:05:57.820
Is this who you talked
about before, that...?

00:06:04.040 --> 00:06:05.510
Rook!

00:06:07.010 --> 00:06:08.930
Rook, Rook!

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:11.230
You surprised the hell out of me, fool!

00:06:11.230 --> 00:06:12.390
Sorry about that.

00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:13.870
How many years has it been?

00:06:13.870 --> 00:06:15.760
Uh, n-nine years, maybe.

00:06:16.330 --> 00:06:19.500
Well? What are you doing here?

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:22.440
You didn't come just to see me, did ya?

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:25.690
Actually, I did.

00:06:26.230 --> 00:06:27.360
For real?!

00:06:27.960 --> 00:06:31.270
Yes. You've been chosen as a short-term

00:06:31.270 --> 00:06:34.520
exchange student at England's Crossfield Academy.

00:06:34.520 --> 00:06:37.500
And I've come here to get you.

00:06:38.220 --> 00:06:43.630
Still, I never imagined you
and Kaito knew each other.

00:06:43.930 --> 00:06:45.760
I've talked about him, right?

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:48.640
A guy in England who
makes awesome puzzles.

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:52.000
This is that awesome dude!

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:53.600
I'm no match for you, Kaito.

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:55.250
The hell are you talking about?!

00:06:58.930 --> 00:07:02.020
Whaaat? England?!

00:07:02.250 --> 00:07:04.550
It ain't all that shocking, is it?

00:07:04.550 --> 00:07:07.280
Goin' there or whatever.
I lived there a long time.

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:09.770
It'll be kinda like visitin' home.

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:13.660
Wouldn't it be better if
your ass just stayed there?

00:07:13.660 --> 00:07:16.450
No, you can't do that!

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:21.340
He is the chief of POG Japan.

00:07:22.600 --> 00:07:23.800
And...

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:26.490
What is the meaning of this?

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:29.520
Phi-Brain development is

00:07:29.520 --> 00:07:32.340
the jurisdiction of us
here in Section Phi.

00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:34.440
Command authority over the

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:38.100
project has shifted
to Director Rook Banjo Crossfield.

00:07:39.310 --> 00:07:41.940
By order of Count Pythagoras,

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:44.150
the director has been given full responsibility.

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:47.610
It looks like you've
made a lot of friends.

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:48.540
What?!

00:07:48.540 --> 00:07:49.640
Friends?!

00:07:49.640 --> 00:07:51.070
That ain't right!

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:53.880
How could me and this fool
possibly look like we're friends?!

00:07:53.880 --> 00:07:56.880
Screw "friends": Me and this guy
ain't even acquaintances!

00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:01.040
Kaito, you and Rook are friends?

00:08:03.060 --> 00:08:04.670
Uh...

00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:07.920
Kaito lost both his parents.

00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:11.810
He was taken in by Baron Kaidou

00:08:11.810 --> 00:08:14.560
and came to study at Crossfield Academy.

00:08:15.590 --> 00:08:16.640
That's where...

00:08:21.490 --> 00:08:24.810
<i>U-Um...</i>

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:25.780
<i>Can we-</i>

00:08:25.780 --> 00:08:26.690
<i>Let's go over there.</i>

00:08:26.690 --> 00:08:28.650
<i>That guy solves puzzles too quick.</i>

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:30.220
<i>It's boring, huh?</i>

00:09:22.600 --> 00:09:24.120
<i>That's cool.</i>

00:09:25.870 --> 00:09:29.270
<i>That's a cool puzzle. Let me try!</i>

00:09:31.480 --> 00:09:35.270
After that, we spent
every lunchtime together.

00:09:37.540 --> 00:09:41.970
I'd make puzzles, and
Kaito would solve them.

00:09:46.060 --> 00:09:48.310
<i>See you tomorrow, Kaito.</i>

00:09:52.250 --> 00:09:55.990
Every time lunch was over,
he'd disappear somewhere.

00:09:55.990 --> 00:09:59.250
It was a boarding school,
but he was in none of the dorms.

00:09:59.250 --> 00:10:01.340
At first, I thought he was a ghost.

00:10:02.140 --> 00:10:03.830
I had a weak constitution,

00:10:03.830 --> 00:10:05.990
so I went to a special annex.

00:10:05.990 --> 00:10:08.360
I was all alone, too.

00:10:09.180 --> 00:10:12.540
I really was glad to have
made friends with Kaito.

00:10:12.820 --> 00:10:17.050
Me, too. But then you transferred...

00:10:17.950 --> 00:10:20.500
I'm glad to see you again, Kaito.

00:10:20.980 --> 00:10:24.610
I can't believe I get to solve
your puzzles again, Rook.

00:10:27.160 --> 00:10:29.440
"The beauty of friendship," huh?

00:10:37.230 --> 00:10:39.070
I'll get in touch with you later.

00:10:39.070 --> 00:10:40.450
Okay. See you.

00:10:43.830 --> 00:10:46.290
I gotta start packing
as soon as I get back.

00:10:46.750 --> 00:10:48.840
Wait! Kaito!

00:10:49.800 --> 00:10:52.960
<i>I've never seen him look so happy.</i>

00:10:55.900 --> 00:11:00.040
<i>I thought I knew everything
about Kaito, but...</i>

00:11:03.150 --> 00:11:04.220
What is it?

00:11:04.770 --> 00:11:09.230
Do Kaito and that boy really get along?

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:12.490
I, Ana, think they're too far apart.

00:11:12.490 --> 00:11:14.470
Kaito is a blue sun.

00:11:14.470 --> 00:11:16.730
That boy is... a red moon.

00:11:18.450 --> 00:11:21.800
Blue sun and red moon?

00:11:26.690 --> 00:11:30.740
To think, Kaito and the
chief are good friends...

00:11:30.740 --> 00:11:32.880
The two were in close proximity.

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:35.000
It's hardly unimaginable.

00:11:35.440 --> 00:11:38.580
But why must Kaito go to England?

00:11:42.040 --> 00:11:45.510
You can become stronger,
more beautiful...

00:11:46.930 --> 00:11:49.950
Let's go together, Kaito.

00:12:01.850 --> 00:12:03.280
He's gone.

00:12:06.410 --> 00:12:09.290
But he can't escape from me.

00:12:12.310 --> 00:12:13.510
Kaito...

00:12:18.370 --> 00:12:19.300
What?

00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:22.300
Nonoha sweets! When did she...?!

00:12:23.140 --> 00:12:25.350
They're even in my vest pocket!

00:12:27.690 --> 00:12:29.770
I-I guess this is from Ana.

00:12:50.190 --> 00:12:51.930
Welcome home, Kaito.

00:12:53.930 --> 00:12:56.960
You, too. Welcome home, Rook.

00:13:00.510 --> 00:13:02.530
That's still there, huh?

00:13:44.390 --> 00:13:45.870
What's this?

00:13:45.870 --> 00:13:48.140
The special annex I spoke of.

00:13:48.490 --> 00:13:49.960
See you tomorrow.

00:14:06.190 --> 00:14:10.160
You were my support. My only one.

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:11.870
It wasn't just me, was it?

00:14:13.310 --> 00:14:15.040
HE was around too, right?

00:14:16.710 --> 00:14:18.040
You're right.

00:14:18.370 --> 00:14:21.340
Say, do you want to go? To that spot.

00:14:21.910 --> 00:14:23.050
"That spot"?

00:14:26.310 --> 00:14:27.770
Where are we going?

00:14:27.770 --> 00:14:29.050
Never mind, just come on!

00:15:04.880 --> 00:15:06.340
This is...

00:15:06.340 --> 00:15:08.250
The church we used to come to.

00:15:25.800 --> 00:15:28.630
<i>This... Is it..?</i>

00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:31.510
<i>Yeah. It's a maze.</i>

00:15:32.880 --> 00:15:34.370
<i>This way, maybe?</i>

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:37.140
<i>No, I think it's this way.</i>

00:15:43.120 --> 00:15:45.440
We challenged this thing
so many times, huh?

00:15:45.440 --> 00:15:48.630
Yeah. We could never quite make the goal.

00:15:48.860 --> 00:15:51.630
One day, we got ourselves lost...

00:15:53.490 --> 00:15:54.950
<i>No crying!</i>

00:15:55.470 --> 00:15:58.480
<i>But if we don't hurry and get back, </i>

00:15:59.140 --> 00:16:00.420
<i>they'll get angry at us.</i>

00:16:02.530 --> 00:16:03.730
<i>Who's there?!</i>

00:16:21.180 --> 00:16:23.000
<i>You.</i>

00:16:24.310 --> 00:16:27.200
<i>It's ME. Have you forgotten?</i>

00:16:28.440 --> 00:16:31.170
<i>This is a strange place
to meet again, huh?</i>

00:16:39.660 --> 00:16:40.680
T<i>his way.</i>

00:16:56.300 --> 00:16:57.480
<i>What is it?</i>

00:16:58.040 --> 00:17:00.700
<i>I've never seen anything like this.</i>

00:17:02.660 --> 00:17:04.380
<i>It's pretty, isn't it?</i>

00:17:08.110 --> 00:17:09.960
<i>Thank you very much.</i>

00:17:12.540 --> 00:17:15.970
<i>I see you haven't given
up on what's dear.</i>

00:17:23.300 --> 00:17:26.060
<i>Um, I'm Kaito Daimon!</i>

00:17:26.060 --> 00:17:27.730
<i>I-I'm Rook!</i>

00:17:29.060 --> 00:17:32.860
<i>I see. Well, I'm Youngster X.</i>

00:17:33.970 --> 00:17:36.360
<i>Y-Youngster X?</i>

00:17:36.640 --> 00:17:38.870
<i>Yup! Sounds cool, right?</i>

00:17:39.760 --> 00:17:42.100
He really was a weird one.

00:17:42.100 --> 00:17:45.180
But he taught us a lot of things.

00:17:49.220 --> 00:17:52.380
<i>Well, it's puzzle time. Let's begin!</i>

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:55.110
<i>Looking at a puzzle tells </i>

00:17:55.110 --> 00:17:57.380
<i>you about the person who made it.</i>

00:17:57.850 --> 00:18:00.500
<i>Encountering a puzzle means
encountering a person.</i>

00:18:01.640 --> 00:18:04.130
<i>Kaito... Solve them. </i>

00:18:04.130 --> 00:18:05.690
<i>Free them.</i>

00:18:05.690 --> 00:18:07.350
<i>
All those unfortunate puzzles.</i>

00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:11.590
It's because he was around that I...

00:18:12.190 --> 00:18:13.320
Kaito.

00:18:14.880 --> 00:18:16.320
What is it?

00:18:16.960 --> 00:18:20.060
Did this route used to be here?

00:18:20.780 --> 00:18:23.550
Uh, I sure don't remember it.

00:18:27.870 --> 00:18:30.160
What is this feeling?

00:18:32.780 --> 00:18:34.250
What's that?

00:18:39.180 --> 00:18:41.930
Let's go back. Something feels strange.

00:18:42.450 --> 00:18:45.090
This might be a Philosopher's Puzzle.

00:18:45.090 --> 00:18:46.710
That would mean it's dangerous.

00:18:46.710 --> 00:18:49.480
A Philosopher's Puzzle? You mean...

00:18:49.480 --> 00:18:50.710
You know about them?!

00:18:50.710 --> 00:18:51.940
Just the rumors.

00:18:53.300 --> 00:18:55.190
They're barriers that long ago,

00:18:55.190 --> 00:18:57.800
those in power sealed their riches inside.

00:18:58.770 --> 00:19:01.510
They contain the desire that one day,

00:19:01.510 --> 00:19:05.280
the right person will come along and obtain the prize.

00:19:07.280 --> 00:19:09.960
But why would they be dangerous?

00:19:09.960 --> 00:19:16.170
Some of them are like pure evil,
made only to hurt people!

00:19:16.170 --> 00:19:18.080
But that's so that the prize doesn't go

00:19:18.080 --> 00:19:19.930
to the wrong person, right?

00:19:20.390 --> 00:19:22.910
It can't be helped that
they're dangerous.

00:19:22.910 --> 00:19:25.850
You ain't never solved one,
so you're not one to talk.

00:19:26.320 --> 00:19:28.110
But YOU have, Kaito?

00:19:28.110 --> 00:19:30.060
I've almost died plenty of times.

00:19:30.690 --> 00:19:33.360
And all of them brimmed with evil?

00:19:34.390 --> 00:19:36.430
W-Well...

00:19:36.430 --> 00:19:38.860
I told you long ago, didn't I?

00:19:38.860 --> 00:19:41.020
It's not the puzzle that's bad.

00:19:41.590 --> 00:19:42.670
Do you remember?

00:19:46.010 --> 00:19:48.350
<i>It's not the puzzle that's bad.</i>

00:19:48.350 --> 00:19:49.850
<i>The one who betrays you is always</i>

00:19:49.850 --> 00:19:51.820
<i>
the human who made it.</i>

00:19:52.880 --> 00:19:55.950
If an honest person makes
a Philosopher's Puzzle,

00:19:55.950 --> 00:19:57.910
there will be no problem, right?

00:19:57.910 --> 00:20:01.380
But still... A puzzle that
hurts people is just-

00:20:01.380 --> 00:20:02.410
Let's try solving it.

00:20:02.410 --> 00:20:03.620
Stop!

00:20:03.620 --> 00:20:05.510
It may not be a dangerous puzzle.

00:20:05.510 --> 00:20:07.510
And what if it IS dangerous?!

00:20:08.130 --> 00:20:12.160
Didn't you make a promise to
solve puzzles you come across?

00:20:12.160 --> 00:20:14.350
To set them free?

00:20:14.350 --> 00:20:16.730
You promised that, didn't you? To him.

00:20:18.310 --> 00:20:21.560
This puzzle may be waiting, too.

00:20:21.560 --> 00:20:23.280
Waiting for someone to solve it.

00:20:24.580 --> 00:20:26.800
It's the human who is evil.

00:20:26.800 --> 00:20:28.290
The puzzle bears no guilt.

00:20:30.560 --> 00:20:31.790
Let's solve it.

00:20:32.180 --> 00:20:33.250
Kaito...

00:20:35.500 --> 00:20:37.470
Let's set this puzzle free.

00:20:43.640 --> 00:20:45.640
Puzzle time... Let's begin.

00:20:47.980 --> 00:20:51.440
Rook! Where are you? Rook!

00:21:21.440 --> 00:21:22.590
This way?!

00:21:24.970 --> 00:21:27.260
Dammit! I've got no time to think!

00:21:27.260 --> 00:21:29.720
It won't even let me go back!

00:21:35.630 --> 00:21:39.420
I've received word from a member of
Section Phi England.

00:21:39.890 --> 00:21:42.210
It would seem Kaito is inside a puzzle.

00:21:42.210 --> 00:21:44.130
A Philosopher's Puzzle?

00:21:44.130 --> 00:21:45.140
No.

00:21:46.760 --> 00:21:48.450
Then what...?

00:21:52.140 --> 00:21:55.460
What is this? This murderous intent?

00:21:56.130 --> 00:21:59.480
It's different somehow from
the other Philosopher's Puzzles!

00:22:01.160 --> 00:22:04.630
It is a dreadful, forbidden puzzle, made

00:22:04.630 --> 00:22:07.850
especially for cultivating the Phi-Brains.

00:22:09.370 --> 00:22:11.000
That's the goal?!

00:22:20.920 --> 00:22:22.300
Where am I?

00:22:24.840 --> 00:22:26.870
It is the Puzzle of Fools.

00:22:37.240 --> 00:22:41.540
Tsukue no ue de umareta sekai
A world born on top of a desk

00:22:41.540 --> 00:22:47.340
Ichiban saki ni kimi ni misetakatta
I wanted to show it to you first of all

00:22:47.770 --> 00:22:52.090
Karappo no heya sotto nukedashite
I sneaked silently out of that empty room

00:22:52.090 --> 00:22:57.210
Hashirihajimeteta
And started running

00:22:58.290 --> 00:23:02.610
Iki hazumasete oka o noboru to
Breathing heavily, I climbed the hill

00:23:02.610 --> 00:23:08.220
Kimi ga saki ni tsuite matte ita ne
And you were already there, waiting

00:23:08.900 --> 00:23:13.160
Takusan no hajimete kimi to mitsuketa
There were so many treasures that I first

00:23:13.160 --> 00:23:17.910
Takaramono datta
Discovered with you

00:23:18.410 --> 00:23:24.020
Kanashisa de afureta toki wa
That time when I was overcome with sadness

00:23:24.020 --> 00:23:26.600
Nanimo iwazu ni tada
You said nothing

00:23:26.600 --> 00:23:29.250
Soba ni ite kureta ne
Just stayed there by my side, didn't you?

00:23:29.250 --> 00:23:33.910
Imademo wasurenai yo
Even now, I haven't forgotten

00:23:33.910 --> 00:23:39.180
Mata aou ne, yakusoku o shiyou
Let's meet again, let's make it a promise

00:23:39.180 --> 00:23:44.400
Kei wa shinai, ano hi no sayonara
It won't fade, the "goodbye" of that day

00:23:44.400 --> 00:23:50.050
Boku no subete, kimi ga kureta michi
Everything I have, the path you gave me

00:23:50.050 --> 00:23:58.960
Zutto kokoro no naka hikaru yo
Will always shine within my heart

00:24:02.500 --> 00:24:06.960
Kaito. I really was glad
to have you as a friend.

00:24:07.220 --> 00:24:09.590
We were birds of a feather.

00:24:09.590 --> 00:24:12.510
I truly believed it back then.

00:24:12.850 --> 00:24:15.910
But it seems you've become unable to see

00:24:15.910 --> 00:24:18.150
the errors you've committed.

00:24:18.560 --> 00:24:20.840
Next time, "The Tower of Parting"

00:24:21.480 --> 00:24:24.670
I can make you stronger, more beautiful.

00:24:21.920 --> 00:24:27.170
The Tower of Parting

00:24:24.670 --> 00:24:26.500
Let's go together, Kaito.
